course: dictionary
lesson: 13064
title: Pretending: the word feigning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To feign something means to pretend that a feeling, illness or state is real when it is not. Feigning is the -ing form of feign, so it describes someone who is pretending right now. «Mia was feigning sleep so her brother would stop talking.» Her eyes were shut, but she was not really asleep. The sentence tells you why: she wanted her brother to think she was asleep.
explain: Look at the words around feigning for clues. «Tom was feigning a sore leg to miss the football match.» If Tom wants to miss the match, his leg is probably not really sore. Ask yourself: is this real, or is someone just acting? Then swap in pretending: «Tom was pretending a sore leg» still makes sense, so feigning means pretending.
explain: Feelings can be feigned too. «Anna was feigning surprise when we shouted "Surprise!"» She already knew about the party, but she acted shocked. Feigning is a more formal word. In everyday talk, we say pretending.
fact: Feign means to pretend a feeling, illness or state that is not real.
fact: Feigning is the -ing form of feign: feign, feigns, feigned, feigning.
fact: Some animals feign death: the opossum plays dead to escape a predator.
fact: Everyday words for feigning are pretending and acting.
fact: Context check: swap in pretending. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «Ben was feigning sleep on the sofa.» What is Ben doing? | Really fast asleep | Cooking his supper | *Pretending to be asleep | Looking for his bed
exercise: «The opossum was feigning death on the path.» What does feigning mean here? | Eating a big meal | *Pretending to be dead | Running very fast | Looking for food
exercise: «Sara was feigning a headache so she could leave the test early.» Why was Sara feigning? | *She did not really have a headache | She wanted to sing | She had a real headache and needed medicine | She was tired after a long walk
test: «Mum was feigning anger, but she was smiling behind her hands.» Which word means the same as feigning? | Sleeping | Hiding | *Pretending | Shouting
test: «The fox was feigning a limp so the hunter would follow it away from its cubs.» What is the fox doing? | Running for home | *Pretending to be hurt | Really hurt and crying | Searching for food
exam: «Liam was feigning interest in the boring film, but he kept checking his phone.» What does feigning mean in this sentence? | *Pretending to be interested | Falling asleep | Asking for a snack | Really enjoying the film
